  "term": "African trypanosomiasis",
  "definition": "African trypanosomiasis is a parasitic disease caused by Trypanosoma brucei and spread by flies in parts of Sub-Saharan Africa. In addition to fever, pain, and swollen lymph nodes, it can harm the brain and later cause confusion, disturbed sleep-wake patterns, and mental decline, with possible progression to coma and death if untreated.",
